# mux-solo: command prefixes that get a status dot in the tmux window list.
# Copy to ~/.config/mux-solo/processes and edit. One prefix per line.
#
# Before matching, your shell aliases are expanded and leading env
# assignments (FOO=1) are stripped. A line matches when the command
# equals it or begins with it followed by a space:
#   rails              -> `rails server`, `rails console`
#   bundle exec rails  -> `bundle exec rails db:migrate`
#   bin/dev            -> `bin/dev`
# So `rs` (aliased to `rails server`) matches the `rails` line below.
# After editing, run `mux-solo-reload` in existing shells.

rails
bundle exec rails
ruby
bin/dev
puma
sidekiq
node
vite
npm
yarn
pnpm
webpack
jekyll
rspec
jest
vitest
